{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: Toolformer API-call filtering. I need to implement a `solve(case)` function in Python.\n\nFrom the candidate artifact description:\n1. For each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least 1)\n3. Accept if parseable=True AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted_call_ids and per-call diagnostics\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\n- `normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens`\n- Accept if `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of call_ids where accepted=True, in order\n- `diagnostics`: list of {call_id, normalized_gain, accepted} for each call, in original order\n\nLet me verify with fixture case 0:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.94835097, loss_with=0.38569502, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595\n  - normalized = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119\n  - accepted: True (parseable and \u003e= 0.05)\n- call1: 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, /4 = 0.09449076, accepted: True\n- call2: 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, /6 = 0.12425022, accepted: True\n- call3: 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, /5 = 0.1519079 - wait, let me recalc: 0.75953930/5 = 0.15190786, accepted: True\n- call4: 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, /5 = 0.04196760, threshold=0.05, 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05, not accepted\n- call5: 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, /4 = 0.19098304, accepted: True\n\nThe description mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round normalized_gain to some reasonable precision. The schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` so it's just a float. Let me round to 8 decimal places or use round().\n\nActually the description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round to a reasonable number. Let me check if there's a specific rounding requirement... It just says \"rounded\". I'll round to 8 significant figures or just leave it as-is. Actually, I'll just compute it and round to maybe 8 decimal places.\n\nWait, looking at the description more carefully: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - This could mean round to some number of decimal places. I'll use round(value, 8) to be safe, or just leave as the computed float.\n\nActually, I'll just return the computed float without explicit rounding since the schema says `\"type\": \"number\"`.\n\nNow, the description mentions \"normalized_weights, stronger_counterfactual, inclusive_threshold, stable_order\" as hard contracts. Let me think about these:\n- `normalized_weights`: normalize by prediction tokens (which we're doing)\n- `stronger_counterfactual`: use the stronger counterfactual - this might mean we consider the maximum gain among multiple counterfactuals? But each call only has one pair of losses...\n- `inclusive_threshold`: the threshold check is inclusive (\u003e= threshold), not strictly greater\n- `stable_order`: maintain original order\n\nThe \"stronger_counterfactual\" is a bit unclear with just one loss pair per call. It might mean: gain = max(0, loss_without - loss_with) - but that would just be the normal gain since we expect positive gain. Or maybe it's already just using the single counterfactual we have.\n\nI think the description is just confirming properties of the algorithm:\n- We use the \"stronger\" (better) counterfactual comparison (loss reduction)\n- The threshold is inclusive (\u003e=)\n- Order is stable\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Normalize by at least 1 token\n        denom = max(1, tokens)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / denom\n        \n        # Accept if parseable and normalized gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me verify case 002 with call4 which has parseable=false:\n- call4: parseable=false, so accepted=False regardless of gain\n\nThe output needs to be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me finalize and encode properly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    if threshold is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold is required\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id must be a string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be numeric\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be a boolean\\\")\\n\\n        # Normalize by at least 1 prediction token (stronger counterfactual, normalized weights)\\n        denom = max(1, tokens)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / denom\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 8),\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01JTbj9Ve2J4Ok9EgzlfUL3K","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2453,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":66,"output_tokens":1814,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1381},"service_tier":"standard"}}